# Ali from Cairo replaces only the life loss damage dealt to its controller causes, never a gain or another loss, and
# lowers that loss at most to none (CR 120.3a, 614.1a; the rulings: life loss bypasses the floor). Bot1, at 2 life, blocks
# one of Bot2's five attacking Memnites with Ajani's Sunstriker (lifelink) while Bot2 controls Tainted Remedy ("If an
# opponent would gain life, that player loses that much life instead"). The combat damage event's results for Bot1 are
# [lose 4, gain 2], and Bot1 orders the two effects on them (CR 120.4c, 616.1). Bot1 applies Tainted Remedy first: the
# results become [lose 4, lose 2], which would take Bot1 to -4, so Ali's floor applies to the damage's loss, but it can
# only lower it to 0, not turn it into a gain: Tainted Remedy's loss of 2 still leaves Bot1 at 0, and Bot1 loses (CR
# 704.5a). (Ali first would make the loss 3, then Tainted Remedy's 2: -3. A floor that turned the loss into a gain of 1
# would meet Tainted Remedy again, a new event to it: -1.)

